[0.0, "o", "\u001b[1;36m  zfsify  ⚡  Ubuntu → ZFS\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[1;36m[1. Scan disk + choose method]\u001b[0m | 2. Prepare disk | 3. Convert ext4 to ZFS | 4. Finish disk + boot setup\r\n  5. Snapshots + recovery + growth\r\n\r\n  Scan Ubuntu, boot configuration and disk layout\r\n\r\nDetected Ubuntu 24.04 | arm64 | uefi boot\r\nRoot filesystem: /dev/vda1 on /dev/vda | used 19.22% (2184208384 / 11362635776 bytes)\r\nPreserved Ubuntu boot arguments: console=tty1 console=ttyAMA0\r\nCPU/PCI/I/O/display kernel arguments and existing sysctl/modprobe configuration are retained.\r\nActive network links/addresses are captured for the RAM rescue; installed network configuration is preserved.\r\nlo               UNKNOWN        127.0.0.1/8 ::1/128 \r\nenp0s4           UP             10.0.2.15/24 metric 100 fec0::5054:ff:fe12:3456/64 fe80::5054:ff:fe12:3456/64 \r\nMake a full offsite backup before proceeding. Conversion can destroy data.\r\n"]
